/* MvStateView — full-bleed error / offline / empty state.
 * Spec: DESIGN_IMPLEMENTATION.md §6 row 6, §8.7.
 * Figma: `Screen 14 - SOS` 79:1304 (error) and 81:1403 (offline) — 390x880,
 * centred illustration group 261x286 with a 46x46 status icon whose vector is
 * 38x38, a 336x50 text frame (title 18/700, body 14/400, gap 8, xCENTER) and a
 * bottom-anchored 358x47 filled button at r14 with a 16/700 label.
 *
 * NOTE: no hex literals anywhere in this file, comments included —
 * TokenDisciplineTests.ComponentUss_HasNoHardcodedColors scans the raw text.
 *
 * WIDTH AND OUTER PADDING ARE THE CALLER'S — same rule as MvAlertBar
 *   V2's 358dp button is the 390dp screen minus its 16dp gutters, i.e. a property
 *   of the page, not of this view. The view stretches into whatever column it is
 *   given and its button stretches with it, so a screen sets its own gutters once
 *   and a card-sized host gets a correctly narrower state for free.
 *
 * ONE LAYOUT, TWO PLACEMENTS
 *   __content is flex-grow 1 and centred; __footer is flex-shrink 0. In a parent
 *   with a definite height (a screen body) the content takes the slack and the
 *   button lands at the bottom — the Figma frame. In an auto-height parent (a
 *   card, a scroll column) there is no slack to take, so the block collapses to
 *   its natural height and the button follows the body at __footer's margin. No
 *   modifier class, no second code path.
 *
 * WHY flex-shrink IS PINNED TO 0 ON BOTH CHILDREN
 *   Yoga's default flex-shrink is 1, and a panel whose docRoot resolves to height
 *   0 (the themeless PlayMode test panel, a not-yet-laid-out screen) then collapses
 *   explicit child heights to nothing. MdBottomSheet's tests hit exactly this. The
 *   view is measured in screenshots, so it pins the value rather than inheriting it.
 *
 * THE STATUS GLYPH'S GREY IS on-surface-variant AT REDUCED EMPHASIS
 *   V2 paints it in a light grey that is not in the palette (Appendix A.1 maps the
 *   design's two body greys to on-surface-variant and stops there). Rather than
 *   introduce a third grey token for one decorative glyph, the slot takes the body
 *   grey and drops to 0.62 opacity: composited over the page background that lands
 *   within ~6/255 per channel of the designed swatch, and — unlike a fixed token —
 *   it keeps the same *relationship* to the background in the dark theme instead of
 *   needing a hand-picked dark counterpart. `opacity` is on the icon alone, so the
 *   title and body keep their full-strength ink.
 *
 * THE ILLUSTRATION SLOT IS EMPTY BY DESIGN
 *   V2's line-art shark is a raster in the Figma file with no export in this repo,
 *   so the slot is sized by whatever the caller sets and hidden while nothing is
 *   (MvStateView.SetIllustration). Nothing is substituted for it.
 */

.mv-state-view {
    flex-direction: column;
    flex-grow: 1;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    flex-basis: auto;
}

/* Centred block: glyph, illustration, title, body. */
.mv-state-view__content {
    flex-grow: 1;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
}

/* 46dp slot, 38dp glyph — the Figma instance and its vector, 1:1 (§1.2). */
.mv-state-view__icon {
    height: 46px;
    font-size: 38px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    color: var(--md-sys-color-on-surface-variant);
    opacity: 0.62;
}

/* Sized by the asset the caller supplies; scaled down to fit a narrow phone
 * rather than overflowing it. */
.mv-state-view__illustration {
    margin-top: 16px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    max-width: 100%;
    -unity-background-scale-mode: scale-to-fit;
}

/* title-medium metrics (18px / 700 / ls 0) — the typescale class is not applied
 * because the component styles its own parts, as every other Mv* does. */
.mv-state-view__title {
    margin-top: 24px;
    font-size: 18px;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    white-space: normal;
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    -unity-font-definition: url("/Assets/DesignSystem/Fonts/Inter-Bold.asset");
    /* V2 paints this in the brand navy; as ink on a page that is `on-surface`,
     * the same collapse MvOptionCard makes for its label. */
    color: var(--md-sys-color-on-surface);
}

/* body-large metrics (14px / 400 / ls 0). Wraps: pt-BR failure copy grows and
 * UI Toolkit has no line-height (Appendix B). */
.mv-state-view__body {
    margin-top: 8px;
    font-size: 14px;
    letter-spacing: 0;
    white-space: normal;
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    -unity-font-definition: url("/Assets/DesignSystem/Fonts/Inter-Regular.asset");
    color: var(--md-sys-color-on-surface-variant);
}

/* ---- Footer ----
 * Hidden outright when there is no action (MvStateView.ActionText). The margin is
 * the gap that matters in the inline placement; in the full-height placement the
 * centred content has already taken the slack and it is invisible. */
.mv-state-view__footer {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    margin-top: 24px;
}

/* MdButton hugs its label at 40dp and pill radius by default; V2's action is a
 * full-width 47dp bar at r14 with a 16/700 label — the same override
 * ReportScreen.uss makes for the submit button. */
.mv-state-view__action {
    align-self: stretch;
}

/* `align-self: stretch` above only widens MdButton's transparent 48dp ROOT; the
 * visible pill is the __container, which hugs its label inside a row that centers
 * it. Growing the container is what actually produces V2's full-width bar. */
.mv-state-view__action .md-button__container {
    flex-grow: 1;
    height: 47px;
    /* Not a stadium: V2 draws r14 here. Half-height would be 23.5. */
    border-radius: var(--md-sys-shape-corner-medium-increased);
}

.mv-state-view__action .md-button__label {
    font-size: 16px;
    -unity-font-definition: url("/Assets/DesignSystem/Fonts/Inter-Bold.asset");
}

/* ---- Variants ----
 * The two designed frames differ by glyph alone, so the modifiers carry no paint
 * today. They exist so a caller can target one (`.mv-state-view--offline .…`) and
 * so tests can assert exactly one is present, the MvAlertBar/MvOptionCard pattern.
 */
